  "method": "Native G11 original-pixel measurements of the physical grey/brown shore stroke. Shape-preserving PCHIP by cumulative guide arclength, sampled at <=2 native px. The Murai mouth/north-head interval between the two open arcs is retained from the existing source outline rather than replaced through an uncertain coastal/marsh boundary. The long northern arc begins at source shore [1394,2300]; its earlier trial hook at [1377,2340] was discarded after 12× source inspection placed that hook inside green/contour ink. Northern arc ends exactly at the mainland Sungei Buloh west-mouth shared junction [2325,1628]. Additional southern-western mangrove and Telok/Kope cape shores, Kranji east outer shore, and the Buloh–Kranji mouth shoulder are direct physical-bank observations from 4–8× native source crops; grid/contour ink and detached brown foreshore islets are excluded. Buloh–Kranji shared endpoints [2478,1644] and [2641.47,1799.05] are retained exactly.",
  "limits": "No new source or registration. Source-generalised and approximate. Blue diagonal forest and horizontal mangrove hatch remain land. Sarimbun: marsh hatch/cream intervals and single drainage strokes do not independently qualify a paired estuary; retained outer shore is not claimed as a reconstructed creek. Perampat: adjacent narrow pale corridor and dark single stream/road strokes do not independently establish paired banks; no inland water branch is inferred. Existing approximation note remains. Murai mouth and north-head coast through source y2300 are deliberately retained unchanged because their paired closure/blurred bank junction was not independently qualified; no claim of complete Murai reconstruction. P. Buloh island is not connected to this mainland arc. The added western arc stops at [1190,2933], before the large red 20/Berih lettering obscures the north shoulder: the obscured interval and Berih interior remain the existing source outline. The Telok/Kope arc begins on the independently visible southern shoulder, so no hidden Berih channel curvature is fabricated. The Kranji east outer arc ends before the causeway at [3222,1714]; no transport line is classified as shore."
}
